Gotansha
Publishing

00:14:48.040 --> 00:14:51.580
I always end up thinking... "Kobu-chan won't mind."

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:55.510
Okay, so... which do you think would fit in?

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:57.580
Hmm... that's tough.

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:00.710
Tanaka must be thinking the same thing.

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:08.300
Furaiden is good. I don't like how plain
their white miso tastes, but they'd rank on this list.

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:11.420
Okay, how about this place called Bonbori?

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:13.290
The quality there has taken a drop recently.

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:16.170
It got too popular after
the owner was featured in the media,

00:15:16.170 --> 00:15:18.210
and now he's got part-timers making the food.

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:20.620
What's the flavor like?

00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:22.290
That jerk...

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:23.420
Hey, you.

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:27.880
Go eat it for yourself.

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:42.750
I get indigestion easily.

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:47.080
Listen up...!

00:15:47.080 --> 00:15:48.330
Sugawara-san.

00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:49.750
The senior editor is calling for you.

00:15:50.380 --> 00:15:51.550
I'll be right there.

00:15:54.170 --> 00:15:57.050
Um... the next one is...

00:15:57.040 --> 00:15:57.960
Tanaka.

00:15:58.580 --> 00:15:59.710
What's up?

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:01.830
Sugawara-san is right.

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:02.830
You need to go eat some for-

00:16:02.830 --> 00:16:05.750
Matsukata-san, Narita-san wants to see you.

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:07.460
In meeting room 3.

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:09.500
Okay...

00:16:12.790 --> 00:16:15.750
Meeting in Progress

00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:18.870
D-dropped out?!

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:22.120
Sasaki the sprinter... Really?

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:26.540
Yep. Broke her leg and was
taken out of the preliminaries.

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:30.090
Everyone thought she was a shoo-in
for the Olympics, but now...

00:16:30.080 --> 00:16:30.710
Sasaki's
athletic affair

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:36.290
Sasaki's
athletic affair
(by Sugawara)

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:34.040
As you know, Sugawara was working
on this scoop from the angle

00:16:34.040 --> 00:16:36.290
of an affair between an Olympian and her coach.

00:16:36.750 --> 00:16:43.040
Now that Sasaki is no longer an Olympian, 2 pages
is too much, so we cut it down to just half a page.

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:46.130
And... what do you want me to do?

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:49.710
Got any ideas to fill space?
That can be done in half a day?

00:16:49.830 --> 00:16:50.660
Impossible!

00:16:50.790 --> 00:16:53.210
Just add extra to one of the articles
currently being written!

00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:55.540
Besides, who can afford
to work on something new?!

00:16:56.750 --> 00:16:59.460
You want an extra page for that ramen article?

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:04.250
Do you think you can make it work
by adjusting the layout of the photos?

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:06.000
Huh?

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:09.670
I already finished the layout
and was about to send it to print.

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:16.010
Uh... well, what I'm asking is not why you won't
do it, but rather how you can get it done?

00:17:16.170 --> 00:17:18.250
It's totally impossible at this point!

00:17:20.210 --> 00:17:23.340
Split the ranking of restaurants
and work it into a chart instead.

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:32.170
If you organize it like that, you can expand it
without the need for new pictures or content.

00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:35.170
How fast can you get it done?

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:37.090
I can do it right now.

00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:41.510
We're counting on you, Kobu-chan.

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:46.580
Tanaka. Search for a chart template in our supplies.

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:48.090
What kind?

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:52.580
For now... just find a few
that we've used in past featured articles.

00:17:52.580 --> 00:17:53.460
Okay.

00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:02.210
Wow, Kobayashi-san is so incredible!

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:08.920
Now then, I'm going to need you
to shift into turbo mode soon, too.

00:18:10.630 --> 00:18:14.380
Accidents and scandals
are the very face of our weekly magazine.

00:18:14.920 --> 00:18:17.670
And the people they involve
are generally considered famous stars.

00:18:18.250 --> 00:18:22.250
But for example, say we cover a porn actress
who lacks any sort of defining trait.

00:18:22.460 --> 00:18:27.460
If she has just one good point, I'll magnify that until
it becomes a strong feature and then write it up.

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:30.330
That's what creativity is all about.

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:32.340
Ramen is no different.

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:34.750
What's important is the ability of the writer.

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:38.510
And in the end, everyone's daily lives
are defined by food and sex.

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:40.660
Because that's human nature.

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:47.960
When I'm done, beer! And a cutlet!

00:18:48.460 --> 00:18:49.750
Curry would be good, too!

00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:52.080
And then ramen, the best for last!

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:53.590
Kobu-chan...

00:18:54.420 --> 00:18:56.710
Work mode... on!

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:11.040
Finally, I have just one more question for you...

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:14.750
I told you before, I approved it
so I'll take responsibility for it!

00:19:24.330 --> 00:19:25.120
Write.

00:19:25.670 --> 00:19:26.460
Chase.

00:19:26.920 --> 00:19:27.920
Research.

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:31.040
The powers of Hataraki Man!

00:19:52.330 --> 00:19:53.210
Did you send that data?

00:19:53.210 --> 00:19:54.210
I'm doing it now!

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:55.170
Once that's done, we're finished.

00:19:58.290 --> 00:19:59.920
That's it. I'm done.

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:02.920
Kobu...

00:20:03.250 --> 00:20:04.210
Kobayashi...

00:20:07.830 --> 00:20:08.660
Huh?

00:20:10.880 --> 00:20:14.170
If you're looking for Kobayashi-san,
he already went home.

00:20:15.710 --> 00:20:18.170
I bet he must have been hungry.

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:21.790
Do you know what restaurant he went to?

00:20:22.250 --> 00:20:25.210
No... I have no idea.

00:20:25.710 --> 00:20:29.290
He said, "I keep the places
that are truly delicious a secret."

00:20:38.790 --> 00:20:39.870
Things like work...

00:20:40.130 --> 00:20:42.880
Pride... manners...

00:20:43.080 --> 00:20:46.660
Enthusiasm... common sense...

00:20:46.670 --> 00:20:47.840
All sorts of things.

00:20:48.580 --> 00:20:50.910
About seventy percent of them are meaningless.

00:20:52.130 --> 00:20:54.010
No, I take that back.

00:20:55.380 --> 00:20:58.380
None of it has to have meaning in the first place.

